.TH CALCULATOR 1 "October 2026" "Calculator 2.0 Alpha 1" "SDE Suite"
.SH NAME
calculator \- the calculator of the Selviana Desktop Environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B calculator
.RB [ --mode " standard|scientific|programmer|converter" ]
.br
.B calculator --eval
.I expression
.RB [ --angle " deg|rad|grad" ]
.br
.B calculator --eval
.I expression
.B --base
.IR hex | dec | oct | bin
.RB [ --bits " 8|16|32|64" ]
.br
.B calculator --convert
.I value from to
.br
.B calculator --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Calculator is a native SDE application with Standard, Scientific,
Programmer and Converter modes and a history of results. Expressions can be
typed or clicked; operator precedence, right associative powers (2^3^2 is
512), unary minus, implicit multiplication (2\(*p, 2(3+4)) and
pocket-calculator percent (200 + 10% is 220) are supported. The result is
previewed while typing; errors such as "Cannot divide by zero" are shown
without clearing the input. Numbers have a 64-bit mantissa and are shown
with 16 significant digits, so 0.1 + 0.2 is 0.3. It works offline.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Enter, =
calculate
.TP
.B Escape, Delete
clear (Delete clears when the cursor is at the end)
.TP
.B Backspace
delete the last character or operator
.TP
.B Ctrl+C, Ctrl+Shift+C, Ctrl+V
copy the result (or the selection), copy the expression, paste
.TP
.B Ctrl+1 ... Ctrl+4
Standard, Scientific, Programmer, Converter
.TP
.B Ctrl+H
show or hide the history
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --mode " name"
Open in a mode.
.TP
.BI --eval " expression"
Print the result and exit. Invalid expressions and domain errors print a
message on standard error and return status 2. The default angle unit is
degrees.
.TP
.BI --angle " unit"
Use deg, rad or grad with --eval.
.TP
.BI --base " base"
Evaluate --eval as a programmer expression in hex, dec, oct or bin.
.TP
.BI --bits " n"
Word size of --base (default 64).
.TP
.BI --convert " value from to"
Convert between units, e.g. "calculator --convert 1 km mi".
.TP
.B --version
Print Calculator's independent SDE build version.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SDE_CALC_QA_FILE
Write the mode, expression, result and error to this file after every
change (for automated tests).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/sde/calculator-history.tsv
the history (last 100 results)
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/sde/calculator.ini
mode, angle unit, base, word size, memory and window size
.TP
.I ~/.config/sde/calculator-currency.conf
currency rates per euro, one "CODE = rate" per line, replacing the offline
sample table
